# Vertical Order Traversal (LeetCode 987)

## Idea

Assign every node

- Row
- Column

Root

Row = 0

Column = 0

Left Child

Row + 1

Column - 1

Right Child

Row + 1

Column + 1

---------------------------------------

## Data Structure

```cpp
map<int, map<int, multiset<int>>> nodes;
```

Meaning

```
Column
   ↓
Row
   ↓
Sorted Values
```

---------------------------------------

## Queue

```cpp
queue<pair<TreeNode*, pair<int,int>>> q;
```

Stores

```
Node

Column

Row
```

---------------------------------------

## Algorithm

1. Push root with (0,0).
2. Perform BFS.
3. Store each node using

```cpp
nodes[col][row].insert(node->val);
```

4. Left child

```
Column - 1

Row + 1
```

5. Right child

```
Column + 1

Row + 1
```

6. Traverse the map and build the answer.

---------------------------------------

## Example

Tree

        3
      /   \
     9     20
          /  \
         15   7

Coordinates

        3 (0,0)

   9(-1,1)   20(1,1)

      15(0,2)  7(2,2)

Output

[
 [9],
 [3,15],
 [20],
 [7]
]

---------------------------------------

## Time Complexity

O(n log n)

---------------------------------------

## Space Complexity

O(n)

---------------------------------------

## Important Points

✅ Use BFS (Queue)

✅ Store Column and Row

✅ Use map to keep columns sorted

✅ Use multiset to sort nodes having same row and column

---------------------------------------

## Pattern

Tree + BFS + Coordinates + Map

Used in

- Vertical Traversal
- Top View
- Bottom View
- Vertical Sum